From fb05d0bdcfc262b022e3d2aa2e7fb1008b6dc918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arch-port <26345330+DrShadow34@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:30:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: v9 texel buffer bounds checks for robustBufferAccess2

Valhall texel buffers (uniform: txf on a buffer view, storage: buffer image
access) are LEA_BUF addresses with converting loads / stores, unchecked.
With buffer robustness (robust_modes ubo / ssbo) the texel address is
checked against the view (coord * stride < size, 64-bit, no division):
past it, reads load from zero-filled memory, so the format conversion
fills in the missing components ((0, 0, 0, 1) without alpha, as
robustness2 wants; a zero result from an OOB address would lose the 1),
and writes / atomics go to an out-of-bounds address, where they are
dropped. The zero memory is load_ro_sink_address_poly, a common sysval
now: the device's zeroed null index buffer on v9 (poly's index buffer
sink reads it too), PAN_SHADER_OOB_ADDRESS elsewhere.

CTS robustness2 (1/20): 699 pass, 0 fail (texel buffers: 111 fail before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013fD3if93WntovhmD8fGa8C
